# Context-scoped ignore for repo-root-context image builds
# (docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile.{admin,web} .). The context must be the
# repo root (pnpm workspace: root lockfile + the @memo/* packages the apps
# import), so this keeps the upload to manifests + sources: everything else
# is either rebuilt inside the image (node_modules, .next, dist) or
# irrelevant to it (backend, docs, e2e artifacts). Env files are excluded on
# purpose — Next loads .env* at build time and a stray local one would
# silently alter the bake; the only env that enters the builds is the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* build args.
.git
.worktrees
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.vercel
package-lock.json
**/package-lock.json
.env*
**/.env*
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
backend
docs
sketches
frontend/admin/e2e
frontend/admin/__tests__
frontend/admin/playwright.config.ts
frontend/admin/vitest.config.ts
# web sources ARE baked into the web image (Dockerfile.web), so unlike the
# admin-era ignore they stay in the context — only its test/e2e artifacts and
# SCRATCHPAD are pruned. All package.json manifests must stay visible: pnpm
# resolves the whole workspace graph (frontend/*).
frontend/web/SCRATCHPAD.md
frontend/web/e2e
frontend/web/test
frontend/web/playwright.config.ts
frontend/web/vitest.config.ts
